DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261202
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261203
SUMMARY:Chief Judicial Magistrate\, Pilibhit: The application of Kumud Gang
 war\, a former state general secretary of the Congress\, under section 173
 (4) of the Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita against the former District 
 Election Officer of Pilibhit\, Gyanendra Singh\, and six others\, over the
  alleged changes to the roll of Pilibhit Sadar
DESCRIPTION:The application of Kumud Gangwar\, a former state general secre
 tary of the Congress\, under section 173(4) of the Bharatiya Nagarik Surak
 sha Sanhita against the former District Election Officer of Pilibhit\, Gya
 nendra Singh\, and six others\, over the alleged changes to the roll of Pi
 libhit Sadar. The District Magistrate's inquiry report and the station hou
 se officer's report are due by this date\, the next date in the case. The 
 magistrate\, Mangal Dev Singh\, registered the application as a miscellane
 ous case on 18 November and issued notices to the seven named. He sought a
  report on the former District Election Officer from the divisional commis
 sioner\, directed the District Magistrate of Pilibhit to hold a preliminar
 y inquiry into the other public servants named and report\, and asked the 
 station house officer to report whether any case has been registered in th
 e matter. Court: Chief Judicial Magistrate\, Pilibhit. Source: Hindustan T
 imes\, https://www.hindustantimes.com/cities/lucknow-news/sir-row-pilibhit
 -court-seeks-inquiry-reports-on-plaint-against-ex-deo-others-1017950214323
 62.html More: https://offtheroll.in/india/disputes/#d-up-44
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://offtheroll.in/india/disputes/
END:VEVENT
